# Raw load-test measurement artifacts are working data, never committed.
# A run produces thousands of per-cell files (SIPp traces, CSVs, JSON
# reports) that are noise in review and bloat every clone. The durable
# record of a series is its written report in docs/; raw artifacts stay in
# storage/app/load-tests/<series>/ (already ignored below) or on the host
# that produced them.
# Load-test run data: per-cell fragments stay out of git — there are thousands
# of them and they would pollute the commit history — but the useful,
# cross-scenario-comparable data is consolidated into a few files under
# results/consolidated/ and versioned: per-cell metrics, per-service CPU/RAM,
# and per-call setup latency. Full raw runs are archived locally outside
# version control.
/load-testing/results/**
!/load-testing/results/consolidated/
!/load-testing/results/consolidated/**
/storage/app/load-tests/
/custom-modules/*
!/custom-modules/.gitkeep
rr
